  "deathBeat": [
   "d8: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Amara Meyer is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
   "d8: 🕯️ Amara Meyer is dead — the arena. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
   "d8: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Giuseppe is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
   "d8: ◈ CRISIS — THE FIRST GRAVE. Giuseppe is dead. The village digs its first grave, and everyone understands at once: this place can kill you. It just did."
  ],
  "recoverHome": [
   "d9: That night, they bring Amara home. Nobody asks you to help carry; nobody has to. By morning the grave is dug by the fire, and the body is laid out beside it. The filling of it is yours."
  ],
  "vouch": [],
  "systemVoice": [
   "d8: SYSTEM: \"Perimeter violated! This is unprecedented! ...Is this unprecedented? Checking. Yes. Unprecedented.\"",
   "d8: SYSTEM: \"INTRUDER REPELLED. The pantry’s aroma is now classified as a defensive liability. The audience is chanting the defenders’ names. Fan clubs are forming. This is how it starts.\"",
   "d8: ◈ THE SPARK — something clicks. A trick Dorothy learned long ago suddenly has edges it never had. SYSTEM: \"ANOMALY: organic unit demonstrates pattern recognition. Slot capacity increased. We are taking notes.\" (Ability slots: 3)",
   "d8: ◈ AUDIENCE TRIAL — SYSTEM: \"The audience wants an encore. A trial, then — smaller this time, but televised.\" Fully identify 3 plants (knowledge level 3) within 3 days. Reward: integration, and a lesson.",
   "d8: ◈ ARC III — ENGINES. SYSTEM: \"VIEWERSHIP MILESTONE. Organic unit demonstrates compounding capability. Resonance protocols unlocked.\" — Your gifts deepen. Used in sequence, they resonate. The village is no longer just surviving. It is becoming something.",
   "d8: ◈ SYSTEM: \"RATINGS DIP. The audience wants STAKES — pointed ones. A PALISADE. Stockpile 14,000 kcal, 350 wood and 60 stone. Walls make such good television. You will thank us when the teeth come.\"",
   "d8: SYSTEM: \"Organic units require fuel. Noting. Noting loudly. The audience is very quiet, which for them is screaming.\"",
   "d8: SYSTEM: \"Oh. Oh no. Was that supposed to happen? The audience is crying. I did not know they could do that.\"",
   "d9: ⬢ SYSTEM: \"Neural depth 52. I can hold more of you now — ability slots: 4.\"",
   "d9: SYSTEM: Naming things. Very human. The audience approves.",
   "d10: ◈ SYSTEM: \"Ooh. NEIGHBORS. You know what neighbors are for? STORYLINES. Go knock — worst case, it's CONTENT. Best case? The show gets BIGGER.\""
  ],
  "burialWindowSay": [
   "d8: The Highbeam Deer thrashes its antlers at you — getting close has a price.",
   "d8: The Highbeam Deer thrashes its antlers at you — getting close has a price.",
   "d8: ◈ The System files the name away with visible satisfaction. It has so few words for things that bleed. (+6 integration)",
   "d8: ◈ CRISIS — THE FIRST GRAVE. Giuseppe is dead. The village digs its first grave, and everyone understands at once: this place can kill you. It just did.",
   "d9: That night, they bring Amara home. Nobody asks you to help carry; nobody has to. By morning the grave is dug by the fire, and the body is laid out beside it. The filling of it is yours.",
   "d10: ◈ The System files the name away with visible satisfaction. It has so few words for things that bleed. (+5 integration)",
   "d11: You say a few words for Amara. Not a ceremony — just: you were here, and someone noticed you leaving. (-3 trauma)",
   "d11: You bury Amara. A marker, of sorts. The village will know where. (+4 trauma)",
   "d12: ◈ The System files the name away with visible satisfaction. It has so few words for things that bleed. (+4 integration)"
  ],
